WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.529
This gate proves the offer is buyable.

00:00:02.529 --> 00:00:03.974
Watching is not enough.

00:00:03.974 --> 00:00:06.502
This lesson is about module offer gate.

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:08.309
Prove the offer is buyable.

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:10.837
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:14.450
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:19.869
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:23.842
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.842 --> 00:00:27.816
Stay practical: self-check offer readiness before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.136 --> 00:00:33.713
Self-check: clear who, specific promise, price you can say, delivery path, and refund rule.

00:00:33.713 --> 00:00:36.103
Remember the objective: self-check offer readiness.

00:00:36.103 --> 00:00:40.484
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.484 --> 00:00:45.265
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:49.646
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:54.426
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.426 --> 00:00:57.215
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:57.215 --> 00:00:58.808
Feedback beats guessing alone.

